# Project: EEJS Portfolio

## Stack
Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, Framer Motion (roaming cursor, project modal and StackForge popup only)

## Architecture
Single-page portfolio on `/` with two personas (developer / Shopify VA); dedicated sub-pages for full content (`/about`, `/projects`, `/experiences`, `/certificates`, `/contact`). Data lives in `lib/data/`.

## Naming & Conventions
- Components in `components/` grouped by `layout/`, `sections/`, `common/`
- Home sections are `Card`s in a bento grid; shared list components in `components/common/` are reused by sub-pages
- Developer copy lives in `lib/data/profile.ts`, VA copy in `lib/data/vaProfile.ts`, and matches the owner's résumé
- CSS design tokens in `app/globals.css` (`--accent`, `--surface`, etc.)

## Design
- Bento cards with icon headings under a profile header; Figma-style roaming cursor that types a note for the section in view
- Geist only; `.chip` for link/tag pills
- Accent (emerald / amber for VA) for hover, active states and the roaming cursor
- Max content width `max-w-4xl`

## What NOT to Do
- Don't add gradient blobs, glows, or scroll-triggered fade-ins
- Don't write marketing copy or claims that aren't on the résumé
- Don't re-enable the Galaxy/Three.js background without explicit request
- Don't scatter copy across components — use the data files
